From a174e3f69b5dd1ab64a6345741ea2f588e1139c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yassin <yassin@Nixos>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 17:24:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 32/37] firmware: qcom: tzmem: disable SHM Bridge on SM6150

Samsung SM6150 secure firmware reports SHM Bridge support, but its
ADSP PAS init-image request subsequently fails with -EINVAL. The working
downstream kernel does not enable SHM Bridge.

Use the generic TZ memory backend on SM6150, as is already required on
the related SDM670 and SM7150 platforms.

Signed-off-by: Yassin <yassin@Nixos>
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_tzmem.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_tzmem.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_tzmem.c
index f926c1f64..c6ab77d8b 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_tzmem.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_tzmem.c
@@ -82,6 +82,7 @@ static const char *const qcom_tzmem_blacklist[] = {
 	"qcom,sc8180x",
 	"qcom,sdm670", /* failure in GPU firmware loading */
 	"qcom,sdm845", /* reset in rmtfs memory assignment */
+	"qcom,sm6150", /* failure in ADSP firmware loading */
 	"qcom,sm7150", /* reset in rmtfs memory assignment */
 	"qcom,sm8150", /* reset in rmtfs memory assignment */
 	NULL
